  "body": "### Summary\n\nLOT-120 (#211: maintenance, about and static pages) may start before capture #298 lands (operator decision, 2026-10-29). Only its About links to the app's HFR topics depend on #298. Until then the lot builds those links as legacy does and lists #298 as *pending capture*. When #298 lands, this review checks the merged lot against the capture and fixes any difference.\n\n### Scope\n\n- **What #298 settles for LOT-120:** how HFR answers the topic id-form link and a stale slug, logged out and logged in. This applies to the About links (operator comment of 2026-10-28 on #211 and its acceptance criteria).\n- Add a test of the About links on the new fixtures.\n- If the capture contradicts the link form the lot chose, fix the lot.\n- Update the LOT-120 spec (\"Pending capture\") and HFR-PROTOCOL §6c.\n- If the capture confirms the choice, close this issue with a comment naming the fixtures and the test.\n\n### Protocol for whoever claims LOT-120\n\nComment here once, from the lot's session:\n- **If you are a CLI session with capture access** (the maintainer's Mac, LOT-001 kit): do #298 first, then name the capture PR and the fixture ids.\n- **Otherwise:** state:\n  - the link form the lot uses, with the legacy file:line;\n  - where the spec lists the pending capture;\n  - the lot's PR.\n\n### Depends on\n\n- #298 (capture)\n- LOT-120 (#211) merged\n\n### Acceptance criteria\n\n- [ ] A test of the About links runs on the #298 fixtures, logged out and logged in, and passes. It is shown to fail if the link form is reversed.\n- [ ] The \"Pending capture\" item is removed from the LOT-120 spec (or rewritten with what remains), and HFR-PROTOCOL §6c records the verified fact.\n- [ ] If the user-visible behaviour changes, `docs/CHANGELOG-LEGACY.md` has a row for it.\n- [ ] The PR says `Closes #<this issue>` and `Refs #211`.\n\n### Model\n\nAny reviewer whose model differs from LOT-120's author model (AGENTS.md §6).",
